 ],
 "literal": "The chaplet is the fragrant cassia of the rainy season, and the beautiful / chest-garland is also cassia. / The mount is the pure white bull; the excellent / and glorious banner is also that same bull, they say. / The stained throat, though worn as an ornament, that stain / is also praised by the scripture-chanting sages. / A female form has become one side; that form, / even if he conceals it within himself, he can hide. / The crescent moon has become the ornament of his forehead; that crescent / is also praised by the eighteen hosts of celestial beings. / To all living beings, he is the protection, / holding a water-pot that never knows the drying up of water, / to the one of rare penance, resplendent with hanging matted hair.",
 "translation": "His head-garland is the fragrant cassia of the rainy season, and the garland on his beautiful chest is also cassia. His mount is the pure white bull, and they say his glorious banner is that same bull. His dark-stained throat is worn as an ornament, and that stain is praised by the sages who chant the Vedas. A female form occupies one half of his body; yet, if he chooses, he can conceal that form within himself. The crescent moon is the ornament of his forehead, and that crescent is adored by the eighteen celestial hosts. To the one of rare penance, resplendent with hanging matted hair, who holds a water-pot that never runs dry, and who is the ultimate protection for all living beings.",
 "modern": "தலையில் சூடும் மாலை கார்காலத்து நறுமணமுள்ள கொன்றை மலர்; அழகிய மார்பில் அணியும் மாலையும் கொன்றையே. அவனது வாகனம் தூய வெள்ளை நிறக் காளை; அவனது சிறந்த புகழுடைய கொடியும் அந்தக் காளையே என்று கூறுவர். அவனது கறை படிந்த தொண்டை அவனுக்கு அணிகலனாக விளங்குகிறது; அந்த நஞ்சுக் கறையை வேதம் ஓதும் அந்தணர்கள் போற்றித் துதிக்கின்றனர். அவனது உடலின் ஒரு பகுதி பெண்ணுருவாக (உமையவளாக) அமைந்துள்ளது; அந்த உருவத்தைத் தனக்குள்ளே மறைக்க நினைத்தாலும் அவனால் மறைக்க முடியும். அவனது நெற்றியில் பிறை நிலவு அழகாக விளங்குகிறது; அந்தப் பிறையை பதினெண் கணங்களும் போற்றிப் புகழ்கின்றனர். எல்லா உயிர்களுக்கும் புகலிடமாக விளங்குபவனும், நீர் வற்றாத கரகத்தை ஏந்தியவனும், தாழ்ந்த சடைமுடியுடன் விளங்கும் அரிய தவக்கோலத்தை உடையவனுமாகிய இறைவனுக்கே (சிவபெருமானுக்கே) இப்புகழ் உரியது.",
 "explanation": "This is the invocatory song (Kadavul Vazhthu) of Purananuru, composed by Peruntevanar, praising Lord Siva. The poet describes the unique attributes of Siva, contrasting his terrifying aspects with beautiful ornaments. His head and chest are adorned with fragrant cassia flowers, and his mount and banner feature a pure white bull. His throat, stained blue by poison, is praised as an ornament by Vedic sages, and his body holds a female form on one side which he can conceal at will. With the crescent moon on his forehead, resplendent matted hair, and a water-pot that never runs dry, he stands as the ultimate protector of all living beings.",
